From k370 (secrets worker, 2026-10-31). Without HETZNER_API_TOKEN, ocp hetzner list reads the token from secrets.yaml; on a clone, k370 now unlocks the project key there with a PIN1 prompt. The other PIN-asking commands take --pins-stdin (one line per prompt, for scripts and tests); hetzner list does not, so it cannot be run unattended on a clone.

Done = ocp hetzner list takes --pins-stdin as the other commands do (same option, same semantics), documented in its POD; test that a PIN1 on STDIN gets the listing past the decrypt with a fake transport. Lane: ocp-provider-worker (OCP::Cmd::Hetzner::List). After k370 is committed.

2026-10-31 15:27 Cause: --pins-stdin is declared once, in OCP::Role::Cmd (option pins_stdin, trigger sets $OCP::Password::PINS_STDIN; around parse_options normalizes --pins-stdin/--pins_stdin, k167). OCP::Cmd::Hetzner::List was the only command reachable from ocp that did not consume the role, so 'ocp hetzner list --pins-stdin' died 'Unknown option: pins_stdin'. Fix: List does 'with OCP::Role::Cmd' (reuse, nothing copied) + =opt pins_stdin POD pointing at the role. t/383-hetzner-list-pins-stdin.t: (1) every command reachable from ocp takes --pins-stdin, derived from the command map; (2) on a clone with PIN1 as the one STDIN line: PIN1 asked on STDERR, read off STDIN (Term::ReadKey untouched), listing goes out with the token from secrets.yaml (fake wire as t/373, answers only that token), printed, key cached in .ocp/; also --label ... --pins_stdin; (3) empty STDIN refused by name, no terminal fallback, no request, nothing cached. t/370 run_ocp no longer leaves --pins-stdin off for hetzner list (its comment said the command had none). Also found: t/95's 'every command' subtest lists classes by grepping for "with 'OCP::Role::Cmd'", so it cannot see a command that never consumes the role (how this slipped); t/383 claim 1 closes that, t/95's comment ('cannot quietly miss the flag') stays overstated -- for the test-writer lane, ocp board.

